---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Where Stripe sends somebody back to after paying for a ticket.
//
// ## It makes no claim about the payment, and that is the whole design
//
// **The redirect back from Stripe is not proof of payment.** A tab can be closed before it
// fires, and this URL is one anybody can type. So this page reports nothing about the
// purchase: it does not say a payment succeeded, and — the half that actually costs money —
// **it never says one did not**.
//
// That second rule is the one `/nn/<year>/entry/complete/` was built around: a page that says
// "nothing was charged" when the webhook is merely late sends somebody to pay a second time.
// Here it is enforced by having nothing to get wrong. The page reads no state at all.
//
// ## Why it does not read the recorded state, unlike the race's version
//
// The race's completion page asks `entries.entry_completion_state()` and reports what the club
// has recorded. Doing the same here would mean an eighth anon-callable function in `store`,
// which CLAUDE.md makes a decision somebody takes in a diff rather than a side effect — and
// the confirmation email covers the same ground for a ticket, because a ticket has no start
// list to be on and nothing to check beyond "did the club get my money".
//
// **If this page ever does report state, the rule above comes with it**: only a recorded
// payment may make a positive claim, and no state may make a negative one.
---

<Base
  title="Thank you — SRC Christmas Party 2026"
  description="Your Southville Running Club Christmas party ticket."
>
  <h1>Thank you</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    If your payment went through, a confirmation email is on its way to the address you
    gave.
  </p>

  <p>
    It carries your reference, and it is the thing to keep — bring it, or just give your
    name on the door. If you or anybody you are bringing has dietary requirements, reply
    to that email and let us know.
  </p>

  {
    /* **No negative claim anywhere on this page.** "It has not arrived" is not the same as
      "you were not charged", and a confirmation can legitimately be a few minutes behind a
      payment. Telling somebody to get in touch is the only safe advice here, because the one
      thing that must not happen is a second payment for the same ticket. */
  }
  <p>
    Nothing in your inbox after an hour? Check your spam folder first, then email
    <a href="mailto:info@southvillerunningclub.co.uk">info@southvillerunningclub.co.uk</a>
    rather than buying again — we can find your payment.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/events/christmas-party-2026/">Back to the party page</a></p>

  <footer>
    <p>Southville Running Club.</p>
  </footer>
</Base>
